      'FUE (Follicular Unit Extraction) and DHI (Direct Hair Implantation) are the two techniques used in the vast majority of hair transplants in Türkiye. Both extract individual grafts from the donor area; the difference is how grafts are implanted. Neither is universally "better" — the right choice depends on your hair loss pattern, donor quality and the surgeon\'s assessment.',
      '## How Do FUE and DHI Differ?',
      'In FUE, the surgeon first opens tiny channels in the recipient area, then places the extracted grafts into them. In DHI, grafts are loaded into a pen-shaped implanter (often called a Choi pen) and placed directly, combining channel opening and implantation in one motion.',
      '## Side-by-Side Comparison',
      '| Factor | FUE | DHI |\n| Implantation | Pre-opened channels | Direct with implanter pen |\n| Best suited for | Larger areas, higher graft counts | Density work, hairline detail, unshaven options |\n| Session size | Higher graft counts per session | Typically fewer grafts per session |\n| Shaving | Full or partial shave usually needed | Unshaven/partial options more common |\n| Indicative 2026 price in Türkiye | €1,500–€3,000 | €2,000–€3,500 |',
      'Prices are indicative 2026 ranges for Türkiye and vary by clinic, graft count and package content — always confirm with a written quote.',
      '## Which Technique Do Surgeons Recommend?',
      'As a general pattern: extensive hair loss with a high graft requirement tends to favour FUE, while patients focused on hairline refinement or added density in unshaved areas are often offered DHI. A reputable clinic examines your donor area and hair loss classification before recommending either — be cautious of any provider that promises one technique to every patient.',
      '## What They Have in Common',
      '- Both use your own follicles from the donor area\n- Both are performed under local anaesthesia, usually in a single day\n- [Recovery timelines](/blogs/hair-transplant-recovery-timeline) are similar: scabbing clears in about 10–14 days\n- Transplanted hair sheds first, then regrows over the following months\n- Final results are typically assessed at around 12 months',
      '## How Itinerary of Türkiye Helps',
