      '## Layer 2: Specialised Medical Travel Insurance',
      'A niche but growing market of insurers covers complications of planned treatment abroad — typically emergency treatment costs arising from complications, extended stays, and sometimes repatriation. Standard exclusions still apply to elective revisions and dissatisfaction with aesthetic results. If your procedure is significant, ask your clinic and your own insurer what products exist for your nationality; policies must be arranged before treatment, never after.',
      '## Layer 3: The Complication Protocol',
      '- A named clinic contact reachable after you return home\n- The clinic\'s process for remote assessment (photos, video calls)\n- Which local providers in your home country they cooperate with, if any\n- Who covers what when a complication needs in-person care — in writing',
